.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt CTLOG_STORE_GET0_LOG_BY_ID 3ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm CTLOG_STORE_get0_log_by_id
.Nd Get a Certificate Transparency log from a CTLOG_STORE
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In openssl/ct.h
.Ft const CTLOG *
.Fo CTLOG_STORE_get0_log_by_id
.Fa "const CTLOG_STORE *store"
.Fa "const uint8_t *log_id"
.Fa "size_t log_id_len"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
A Signed Certificate Timestamp (SCT) identifies the Certificate
Transparency (CT) log that issued it using the log's LogID (see RFC
6962, Section 3.2). Therefore, it is useful to be able to look up more
information about a log (e.g.
its public key) using this LogID.
.Pp
.Fn CTLOG_STORE_get0_log_by_id
provides a way to do this.
It will find a CTLOG in a CTLOG_STORE that has a given LogID.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Sy CTLOG_STORE_get0_log_by_id
returns a CTLOG with the given LogID, if it exists in the given
CTLOG_STORE, otherwise it returns NULL.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ct 7 ,
.Xr CTLOG_STORE_new 3
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Fn CTLOG_STORE_get0_log_by_id
function was added in OpenSSL 1.1.0.
